abstract: >
  SolarMap.PH is an open-source pipeline for detecting rooftop solar
  photovoltaic installations from high-resolution public satellite imagery.
  It combines a frozen CLIP-ViT-L image encoder, a logistic-regression
  classifier head, Platt-sigmoid probability calibration, and a SAM-based
  per-building segmentation stage. The shipped classifier is validated at
  F1 = 0.870 (precision 95.9%, recall 79.7%) on an honest 20% held-out
  source-disjoint split, and the build is bit-exact reproducible from
  cached embeddings via a deterministic Docker recipe.
